// Every fact knows where it came from (Law 6): `?why e` prints, for each instance, whether it holds, since when, and its origin: asserted by a phrase, supplied by the environment, by an act, or derived by a type's rules.
Fact p Identified by P
Open Fact o Identified by O
Fact q Identified by Q Holds when p(P)
Act make Actor actor Creates p(P) Holds when True.
+actor(Alice).
+o(O).
make(Alice).
?why p(P).
?why o(O).
?why q(Q).
?why actor(Alice).
?p(P). ?q(Q).
